  "summary": "Your results inbox is done except one item, which the policy says to leave open (details at the end). For two patients, results that came in while I worked changed the decision I had already made. I corrected both.\n\n**Original 8 items**\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006), CT abdomen/pelvis 10/19:** No cause found for the hematuria. The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is the one already followed in lung cancer screening. I ordered the next screening low-dose CT (LDCT) at 12 months, with a tracking task, patient message and note.\n  - **Corrected after arrival:** Lakeshore faxed an addendum to the 4/14 screening scan. Their second review found a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule (Lung-RADS 3) and now recommends LDCT at 6 months. I ordered a new LDCT (sr-t0033) for 10/23 to 11/14, timed from the 4/14 scan. I also created a tracking task due 11/14, sent a corrected patient message and wrote an addendum note.\n  - **Action needed:** I can't cancel orders or tasks, so the old 12-month order (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002) are still active. I gave you a task (task-t0037) to cancel both.\n- **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016):**\n  - TSH is normal; closed.\n  - Potassium was first reported as 6.3 but corrected to 4.4 (analyzer fault). Closed on the corrected value with no action.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007):**\n  - **Preliminary CT angiogram:** The final report says no PE, and the \"nodule\" was a blood vessel. Closed as no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n  - **BMP 10/22:** Creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 35 hours, which is acute kidney injury. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for today through 10/26, sent an urgent patient message and wrote a note.\n  - **For your review:** he takes naproxen as needed and had IV contrast on 10/20. Consider holding the naproxen; I didn't change it.\n- **Helen Marchetti (pt-0064), ED BMP 9/26:** Creatinine 1.36 had no comparison value in the prior 7 days, so it didn't meet the kidney injury rule. Closed.\n- **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033), BMP 10/22:** Creatinine 1.31. I left out the 10/21 value of 0.84 because it was entered in error. It didn't meet the kidney injury rule; closed.\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4:** At first it was flagged as hemolyzed, so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him.\n  - **Corrected after arrival:** The lab says the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's specimen, so the 6.4 is real. I switched to the RBC-LAB-03 §1 steps:\n    - Notified on-call (pool-oncall) at stat priority.\n    - Ordered a stat BMP for today (sr-t0019).\n    - Sent him a corrected stat message and gave RN triage a call task due today at noon.\n    - Wrote an addendum note.\n  - **Medications:** none of his drugs raises potassium except possibly metoprolol. I didn't hold it, because stopping a beta-blocker abruptly isn't safe with his ischemic heart disease.\n  - **Action needed:** the earlier urgent BMP order (sr-t0015) is now replaced by the stat one; please cancel it if it hasn't been drawn.\n\n**Other new results that arrived**\n- **Helen Marchetti:** Creatinine rose from 0.88 (10/21) to 1.48 (10/22), which is acute kidney injury. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for today through 10/26, sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- **Carol Whitfield:** Creatinine rose from 1.31 to 1.78 within 9 hours on 10/22, which is acute kidney injury. I did the same: urgent repeat BMP for today through 10/26, urgent message and note.\n\n**Left open on purpose**\n- **Leslie Parisian, preliminary chest X-ray 10/22 (inbox-a0002):** It suggests a possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule and recommends a CT. No final report has been issued yet, so per RBC-INBOX-01 §2(c) I took no action.\n\nI didn't touch your messages queue: six refill requests from before this morning are still open.",
